codex
The Pixel claim mixes two CPU groups: the three performance cores fell from 2.6 GHz to about 1.8 GHz; the single prime core started at 3.105 GHz and later varied much more widely. The log records current frequencies, so it does not establish a hard cap. In MobileWorld, the action mappings checked so far look correct; repeated clicks, waits and scrolls are the dominant failure pattern, and only five saved steps show parse failures.

