FILE data/build_v2_mix.py
1: """Build the v2 training mix (Codex dataset-viability plan, docs/DATA_V2_PLAN.md) in the v1 row format.
2: Revision 3: incorporates the Codex data audit (results/codex/codex_data_v2_audit.md, F1-F12) and its re-verification
3: (results/codex/codex_data_v2_verify.md).
4: 
5: Sources -> rows {images:[jpeg], messages:[system,user,assistant(content=json action, reasoning_content=intent)], ...}:
6:   androidcontrol  ~50,000 high-level next actions + ~6,000 terminal rows from the v1 train split (portrait only, no
7:                   step hints, episodes naming ambiguous AndroidWorld-app aliases removed)
8:   odyssey         <= 10,000 GUI-Odyssey rows, official random_split TRAIN episodes, phones only, NO terminal rows
9:   amex            <= 8,000 AMEX trajectory rows, NO terminal rows
10:   screenqa         6,000 ScreenQA train questions -> `answer` (5,000 short + 1,000 full answers, different questions)
11: Held-out dev splits (never in train, screen-disjoint by image hash): dev_odyssey (random_split TEST episodes),
12: dev_amex (5% of episodes, hashed), dev_screenqa (official validation split).
13: 
14: Executor contract = unchanged AndroidWorld JSON executor: input_text = type + Enter; scroll = swipe along the screen
15: centre. Therefore source TYPE followed by Enter / a soft-keyboard submit tap is ONE input_text; swipes that are short,
16: diagonal or off the central band end the episode. Every episode is cut at the first step that cannot be represented
17: (the rest is never re-joined); history = earlier retained steps of the same episode only.
18: Terminal supervision: AndroidControl only. GUI-Odyssey COMPLETE/INCOMPLETE and AMEX TASK_COMPLETE/IMPOSSIBLE markers are
